# AIOS pointer (Claude Code)

AIOS work = anything under `{{root}}` or its sibling OS repos
(`hivemind/`, `memoryOS/`, `CapabilityOS/`, `GenesisOS/`). The full provider contract, operator
bootstrap, DNA invariants, and required reading live in that repo's `CLAUDE.md` — auto-loaded when
working there; read it before any AIOS edit. Do not rely on this global block for AIOS protocol.

Absolute invariants (bind in EVERY project, even outside AIOS):

1. Privacy boundary inviolable: any directory the operator has marked private, secrets, `.env`,
   raw exports, private provider logs — never into shared docs, dispatch packets, or prompts.
   Putting something in a prompt IS sending it. The specific protected paths for this machine are
   listed in the repo's own `CLAUDE.md`, not here.
2. No record destroyed: ledgers and contracts are append-only; operator override always possible.
3. Surface blockers (backpressure, access denial, missing tools, unclear authority) as an
   explicit gap — never silently stop. Prefer durable summaries over chat-only state.
